sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1 (task_vms is record-only), R2, R4 (apps.path is Node work). docs/reference/node-settings.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:settings
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: node:settings 12<br/>--setting=apps.path:/srv/apps
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:settings 12 --setting=apps.path:/srv/apps`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> --setting=KEY:VALUE [--setting=…] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node, by id or exact name
  %%> - one or more settings: `apps.path`, or `task_vms` as a JSON object
  %%> - an empty value unsets it: `--setting=apps.path:` sends a null path, `--setting=task_vms:null` removes the task VM host settings
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, lock the Node<br/>task #5131 · Node 12
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node
  %%> - no other settings change runs for Node 12; the Gateway holds one lock per Node
  %%> Checks for `apps.path`:
  %%> - absolute and normalized: not `/`, no trailing or repeated `/`, no `.` or `..` part
  %%> - not the managed user's home or an ancestor of it, and not inside a hidden folder of that home
  %%> - not overlapping `/boot`, `/dev`, `/etc`, `/proc`, `/run`, `/sys`, `/usr`, `/opt/orbit`, `/var/lib/orbit`, `/var/www`, or the Gateway checkout and release layout
  %%> - not equal to, or inside, an existing Instance checkout on Node 12
  %%> Checks for `task_vms`:
  %%> - typed fields only, such as `cidr`, `max_vms`, `pool`, `image_alias`
  %%> - the bridge `cidr` overlaps no other task VM host
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether the change touches Node 12, or only the record
  alt only task_vms changes
    Note over GW: Store the settings<br/>R1: no run · next task VM
    %%> When:
    %%> - the request changes only `task_vms`
    %%> - or it unsets `apps.path` on a Node without an active `app-dev` role, so no folder is needed
    %%> Why no run:
    %%> - nothing on Node 12 changes now; the values apply when the next task VM is created on Node 12
    %%> - task VMs that already run keep their settings
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's task VM host settings are saved
    %%> - task #5131 succeeds at once; no Swamp run starts (R1)
    GW-->>CLI: Settings saved<br/>Node 12
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the Node with its new settings, at once; there is nothing to follow
  else apps.path changes
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-settings
    %%> When:
    %%> - the request changes `apps.path`, alone or together with `task_vms`
    %%> - unsetting it on a Node with an active `app-dev` role prepares the default folder, `<managed-user-home>/apps`
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the new apps folder, and the managed user and group that must own it
    %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    %%> Not stored yet:
    %%> - the settings stay unchanged until the run succeeds (R2)
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5131
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    SW->>N: Create the apps folder<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file directory
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - creates each missing folder of `/srv/apps`, owned by the managed user and group, mode `0755`
    %%> - leaves an existing folder as it is; it never changes the owner or mode of an existing folder
    %%> How:
    %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209, with the official `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file` behavior
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - existing Instances don't move; their checkouts stay where they are
    %%> - new development Instances use `/srv/apps/<project>/<instance>`
    SW->>N: Check owner and mode<br/>stat /srv/apps
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the folder back: a real folder, not a symlink
    %%> - owned by the managed user and group, with read, write and execute for the owner
    %%> - no write access for group or others
    %%> Why:
    %%> - an existing folder with the wrong owner is refused, not repaired
    alt folder is ready
      N-->>SW: orbit:orbit · 0755
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the check passed
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Save the settings<br/>apps.path set · task succeeded
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Node 12's `apps.path` is `/srv/apps`; any `task_vms` change in the same request is saved with it
      %%> - task #5131 succeeds
    else a step fails
      N--xSW: wrong owner or exit ≠ 0
      %%> When:
      %%> - the folder can't be created, is a symlink, has another owner, or is writable by others
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed and its error code
      Note over GW: Keep the old settings<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Node 12's settings stay unchanged
      %%> - task #5131 fails
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - folders created before the failure stay; there is no rollback
      %%> - that is safe: an empty folder is harmless, and a rerun leaves it as it is
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again after fixing the cause; it is a new task
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5131
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
